Sval: test profiles start without Sval's first run, list downloads or HTTPS-Only Mode

Every harness profile starts from testing/profiles/base, so a pref set there
covers every mochitest and xpcshell profile, Mozilla's own tests included.

- First run opens its dialog over the first window of a fresh profile, which
  every harness profile is. A browser-chrome run whose manifest does not turn
  it off then stops at its start: `Tester.nextTest` throws on the selected
  browser and no test begins. Sval's first-run test turns it on for itself.
- The harness crashes on a connection to a real host
  (MOZ_DISABLE_NONLOCAL_CONNECTIONS), and a blocking level would otherwise
  fetch its lists from their publishers. A test that needs a list serves it
  itself.
- HTTPS-Only Mode stops a plain-http load at its warning page, and the
  harness serves its own pages from http://mochi.test:8888, which has no
  secure version, so a run hangs before its first test. Sval's HTTPS-Only
  tests turn it on for themselves.

The harness reads these files from the source tree; no test manifest or
chrome API reaches every profile.

diff --git a/testing/profiles/base/user.js b/testing/profiles/base/user.js
index eb09e84d30..bc43450bea 100644
--- a/testing/profiles/base/user.js
+++ b/testing/profiles/base/user.js
@@ -26,3 +26,18 @@ user_pref("browser.startup.couldRestoreSession.count", -1);
 // This is used to disable address autofill telemetry since we cannot download
 // the model within tests.
 user_pref("extensions.formautofill.useml", false);
+
+// Sval: first run opens a window-modal dialog on a fresh profile, which every
+// harness profile is, and the harness cannot start a test behind it. Sval's
+// first-run test turns it on for itself.
+user_pref("browser.sval.firstRun.enabled", false);
+
+// Sval: blocking lists download from their publishers on a schedule, which
+// the harness forbids (MOZ_DISABLE_NONLOCAL_CONNECTIONS). A test that needs a
+// download serves the list itself.
+user_pref("browser.sval.adblock.updates.enabled", false);
+
+// Sval: HTTPS-Only Mode stops a plain-http load at its warning page, and the
+// harness serves its pages from http://mochi.test:8888, which has no secure
+// version. Sval's HTTPS-Only tests turn it on for themselves.
+user_pref("dom.security.https_only_mode", false);
